<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8"?>
<Defs>

  <!--
    A factory hopper that holds four stacks on its one cell. Everything else is inherited from VFE Factory's
    hopper (Name added by Patches/FactoryHopper_ParentName.xml): its Building_FactoryHopper class (input,
    output and plain graphics, the allow taking and allow inserting toggles), the factory-hopper flag,
    storage group tag, Low default priority, research and Architect tab. Code read 29 Oct 2026, not yet tested
    in game: machines check every item on an input cell (Process.CheckInputSlots), belts fill storage up to
    the cell's maxItemsInCell (Building_Conveyor) and pull the first stack they find.

    Four stacks: one per solid ingredient of a four-ingredient bill, so a surplus stack of one ingredient
    cannot fill the cell and lock another out (same-type items merge into one stack). Cost and work are
    authored (stock hopper: 20 steel, 400 work). Agent defaults, owner to tune.
  -->
  <ThingDef ParentName="PhobosFactory_FactoryHopperParent">
    <defName>PhobosFactory_DeepFactoryHopper</defName>
    <label>deep factory hopper</label>
    <description>A factory hopper with racks inside, so it holds up to four stacks at once instead of one. A machine can draw several different ingredients from this one cell, and a belt keeps filling it until all four places are taken.</description>
    <building>
      <maxItemsInCell>4</maxItemsInCell>
    </building>
    <statBases>
      <WorkToBuild>800</WorkToBuild>
    </statBases>
    <costList>
      <Steel>35</Steel>
      <ComponentIndustrial>1</ComponentIndustrial>
    </costList>
  </ThingDef>

</Defs>
